  "Number": 12,
  "Question": "Suppose the estimated \\(20\\) billion dollar cost to send a person to the planet Mars is shared equally by the \\(250\\) million people in the U.S. Then each person’s share is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$40\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$50\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$80\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$100\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$125\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Equal sharing means dividing the total cost by the number of people. A billion is \\(1000\\) million, so \\(20\\) billion is \\(20{,}000\\) million. Dividing both numbers by one million simplifies the calculation:\n\\[\n\\frac{20{,}000{,}000{,}000}{250{,}000{,}000}\n=\\frac{20{,}000}{250}\n=\\frac{2000}{25}\n=80.\n\\]\nEach person’s share is \\(\\boxed{\\$80}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
